{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"792f6443d24191b5","type":"text","text":"Within Melonia is a council known as The Round Table comprised of 12 wielders of magic all suited to different roles. \n\n\n\nHead chair: [[Alura Vysoren, Cobalt Princess.canvas]] A powerful mage who has a mind designed for political structure and arcana. Alura is the current head of Melvain taking Divinas place and although a leader is kinda hearted wanting to help those around her\n\n\nRest of Chairs:\n\n[[Yelrien Cilindrath (Master of Dark Magic).canvas]]: Dampir Shadow Sorcerecs.\n\n[[Fuxor Granfert.canvas]]: Hald Orc Mage (Kind but cunning)\n\n[[Vaelin Starweaver (Master of Wards).canvas]]: A methodical High Elf Abjuration wizard who oversees the city's magical defenses and shields. Stern, highly protective, and deeply serious about security protocols.\n\n[[Silas Vance (Master of Intelligence).canvas]]: A Tiefling Illusionist who acts as the city's spymaster. Charming but cryptic, he rarely attends meetings in his true physical form, preferring to project intricate illusions.\n\n[[Oona Mossbeard (Warden of the Harvest).canvas]]: A towering Firbolg Druid responsible for the region's agriculture and weather manipulation. Gentle, a bit disorganized, and usually brings dirt and small animals into the council chambers.\n\n[[Kaelen Forge-Born (Commander of the Vanguard).canvas]]: A brash Dwarven Evoker who integrates explosive magic with military tactics. Loud, fiercely loyal, and oversees the training of the city's battle mages.\n\n[[Lady Elara Dawn (High Healer).canvas]]: An Aasimar Divine Soul Sorcerer who manages public health and the city's clerics. Graceful and deeply compassionate, though visibly exhausted by the endless needs of the populace.\n\n[[Gideon Goldvein (Master of Coin).canvas]]: An eccentric, hyperactive Gnome Transmuter. He views economics through the strict lens of equivalent exchange and uses his magic to manage the city's physical infrastructure and resources.\n\n[[Xor'thas the Silent (Keeper of the Archives).canvas]]: A stoic Dragonborn wizard from the Order of Scribes. He possesses a flawless photographic memory, speaks only when entirely necessary, and guards Melonia's deepest historical secrets.\n\n[[Lyra Valerius (Grand Diplomat).canvas]]: A human Bard and Enchanter. Endlessly charismatic and terrifyingly persuasive, she handles foreign relations and trade negotiations, ensuring Melonia gets the better end of any deal.\n\n[[Morven Ash (Speaker for the Fallen).canvas]]: A somber Shadar-kai Necromancer who acts as the city's chief forensic investigator. He breaks typical dark magic stereotypes by using necromancy to solve murders, speaking with victims to ensure justice is served.\n\n\n\n\nIn Favor of Intervention (5 Seats)\nAlura Vysoren (Head Chair): Spearheading the movement. Believes their immense power comes with a moral obligation to protect the vulnerable, even if it threatens their secrecy.\n\nFuxor Granfert: Half-Orc Mage. Kind but cunning; sees isolation as cowardice and worries that ignoring outside threats will eventually let those evils grow strong enough to breach Melonia's hidden borders anyway.\n\nLady Elara Dawn (High Healer): Compassionate to a fault. Witnessing the suffering outside through refugees or scrying has pushed her firmly to Alura's side, arguing that hoarding healing magic while innocents die violates their principles.\n\nKaelen Forge-Born (Commander of the Vanguard): Eager for action. He views the current era as stagnant and believes mages should test their mettle against real threats rather than practicing in a vacuum.\n\nMorven Ash (Speaker for the Fallen): Believes that evil left unchecked in the Material Plane always breeds worse catastrophes. He argues that proactive intervention prevents greater tragedies from reaching their doorstep.\n\n\nOpposed to Intervention (5 Seats)\n\nVaelin Starweaver (Master of Wards): The most vocal opponent of breaking cover. He argues that exposing Melonia to the outside world risks total annihilation, pointing to millennia of careful concealment that kept them safe.\n\nSilas Vance (Master of Intelligence): Prefers shadows and spycraft. He believes intervention will attract the wrong kind of attention from regional superpowers and criminal syndicates, making them targets.\n\nGideon Goldvein (Master of Coin): Purely practical and risk-averse. He calculates that the economic and structural cost of deploying forces externally will drain their resources and destabilize Melonia from within.\n\nXor'thas the Silent (Keeper of the Archives): Historical purist. He leans heavily on historical precedent, arguing that every time hidden societies have revealed themselves to the surface world, it ended in betrayal and slaughter.\n\nLyra Valerius (Grand Diplomat): Outwardly charming, but strategically cautious. She believes they lack the diplomatic infrastructure to intervene cleanly and that entering the fray will entangle them in proxy wars they cannot win.\n\n\nThe Undecided Swing Votes (2 Seats)\nYelrien Cilindrath: Caught between the heavy mantle of historical protection and the undeniable gravity of the outside world's suffering. Leans toward whichever argument presents the most airtight safety guarantees.\n\nOona Mossbeard (Warden of the Harvest): Deeply connected to the natural world. She is torn because nature suffers outside their borders, yet the unnatural chaos of civilization entering Melonia's sanctuary terrifies her.\n\n","x":-1000,"y":-580,"width":1870,"height":1160},
		{"id":"7913a9ce83d7af51","type":"text","text":"[[Melonia]]\n#Melonia ","x":-1000,"y":-700,"width":250,"height":55}
